Designers Comments
==================

The law of diminishing returns was applied to the improvement of coverage for this peripheral,
whereby the extensive man hour effort returned insignificant improvement in coverage. 

The coverage figure of 70% for the SciCntl block is reasonable - this is a state machine which allows
synchronous transactions to intercept the normal asynchrounous card transaction sequences.
To exhaustively cover this block would mean steering it to each state then performing the
synchronous operation ... this was deemed impractical within the time constraints.
The State_Tests were based on original production TIC based sequences and raised the coverage
for the SCiCntl block from 53% to its current figure of 70.1%.

It should also be noted that a 4 bit state machine is a very small amount of logic i.e. four
d-types and the related combinational logic.

Martyn T. Jones
29th November 2001


